==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|de|Schnick, Schnack, Schnuck|Schnick-Schnack-Schnuck|Schnickschnackschnuck}}
* The interjection may also be lowercase.

===Etymology===
Probably from {{m|de|schnicken}}, variant of {{m|de|schnippen|t=to flip one’s fingers}}. The ''i-a-u'' ablaut is very common in German (and beyond); cf. {{m|de||tri-tra-trullala}} etc. Perhaps also influenced by {{m|de|Schnickschnack}}.

